A C++{{ cpp_standard }} library in the [pitchfork layout](https://github.com/vector-of-bool/pitchfork), built with CMake.

## Layout

- `include/{{ package_name }}/` - public headers (the API); `src/{{ package_name }}/` - implementation
- `tests/*.test.cpp` - Catch2 tests (picked up automatically)
- `examples/` - small programs that use the library the way a consumer would
- `docs/` - Doxygen configuration; `cmake/` - vendored CPM.cmake
- `build/<preset>/` - build trees, one per preset in `CMakePresets.json` (`dev`, `san`, `coverage`, `release`)

## Commands

Everything goes through `just` (run `just` to list recipes), which wraps the
CMake presets. Do not invoke the compiler or `make` directly.

- `just check` - format check, clang-tidy, build and tests with warnings as errors. **Work is not done until this passes.**
- `just test-san` - tests under ASan + UBSan; run it after touching memory, lifetimes or arithmetic
- `just cov` - coverage report; `just docs` - Doxygen with warnings as errors
- Dependencies: `CPMAddPackage(...)` with a pinned version, in the CMake file that needs it

## Verification

- A behaviour change needs a Catch2 test in `tests/` that fails before the
  change and passes after.
- Hooks do the routine work: every edit is formatted with clang-format, and
  `just check` runs when you finish. If it fails you get the output; fix the cause.
- Compiler warnings and clang-tidy findings are errors. Do not add `NOLINT` or
  warning pragmas to get green; configure the check in `.clang-tidy` with a reason.
- Prefer clangd (go to definition, find references, diagnostics) over text
  search for navigating C++.

## Gotchas

- A new `.cpp` under `src/` or `examples/` must be added to its target in the
  matching `CMakeLists.txt` (tests are globbed).
- clangd and clang-tidy read `build/dev/compile_commands.json`; `just setup` creates it.
- Dependencies are downloaded once into `.cache/cpm` and shared by all presets.
- `cmake/CPM.cmake`, `build/` and `.copier-answers.yml` are not edited by hand; edits to them are blocked.
